  {
    "date": "2025-04-09",
    "term": "著しい",
    "kana": "いちじるしい",
    "meaning": "remarkable, considerable",
    "level": "N1",
    "pos": ["adjective (keiyoushi)"],
    "priority": ["ichi1", "news2", "nf47"],
    "pitch": [5],
    "stratum": "wago",
    "processes": ["rendaku"],
    "headline": "Ichijirushii began as ichishirushi, 逸 (ichi-, “very”) plus 著し (shirushi), and shirushi was voiced to jirushi by rendaku in the Muromachi period.",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From 逸 (ichi-, “very”) + 著し (shirushi, “clear, obvious, conspicuous”, a ku-adjective)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Attested in the Heian period as a ku-adjective pronounced いちしるし (ichishirushi). Since the Muromachi period, it became pronounced いちじるし (ichijirushi), where the shirushi changes to jirushi as an instance of rendaku (連濁). Since around the Edo period, it changed conjugation class and became a shiku-adjective."
      },
      {
        "quote": "The modern form is from いちじるしき (ichijirushiki), the 連体形 (rentaikei, “attributive form”) of the Late Middle Japanese shiku-adjective いちじるし (ichijirushi), with the medial /-k-/ falling out."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
